# The build context every image is built from (compose: `context: .`). The worker image copies the whole context
# into its runtime layer, so what is left here ships. Patterns are relative to the repository root.
node_modules
.next
.git
var
test-results
playwright-report
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store

# Agent worktrees and local tool state: gigabytes, never part of an image.
.claude

# Documentation, research and evidence screenshots are read by people, not by any image. Nothing at run time reads
# docs/ (agent and skill texts only cite those paths).
docs

# Browser tests and prototype-era tooling run on the host. KEEP tests/unit/: a skill's status is computed at run time
# from whether its `verifiedBy` test files exist (src/server/org/skills.ts computeSkillStatus); without them the
# worker would demote every VERIFIED skill to DRAFT. Also kept on purpose: skills/ (the SKILL.md files the worker
# reads), docker/models/manifest.json (the model registry), drizzle/ (migrations), scripts/ (operations, e.g.
# scripts/studio-intake.ts), src/, public/, tsconfig.json (tsx resolves the @/ alias with it).
tests/e2e
tools
